msgstr ""

#: ../../../deeplearning_operators/matmul_sparse.md:35
msgid "Compress a dense tensor"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deeplearning_operators/matmul_sparse.md:37
msgid ""
"To utilize sparse Tensor Cores, a dense tensor must first be **compressed** "
"into its non-zero values along with the corresponding metadata."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deeplearning_operators/matmul_sparse.md:39
msgid ""
"Both `PyTorch` and `vLLM` use `CUTLASS` as their computation backend (see "
"references [here](https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/blob/"
"a8d6afb511a69687bbb2b7e88a3cf67917e1697e/aten/src/ATen/native/sparse/cuda/"
"SparseSemiStructuredOps.cu#L47) and [here](https://github.com/vllm-project/"
"vllm/blob/a5dd03c1ebc5e4f56f3c9d3dc0436e9c582c978f/csrc/sparse/cutlass/"
"sparse_scaled_mm_c3x.cuh#L116)), leveraging `CUTLASS`’s built-in compressor "
"(or reimplementing it in `PyTorch`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deeplearning_operators/matmul_sparse.md:41
msgid ""
"A compressor is provided with the sparse GEMM example in `examples/gemm_sp/"
"sparse_utils.py`. Pass in a dense 2:4-sparse tensor and optionally a "
"metadata dtype to get back the compressed values and metadata:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deeplearning_operators/matmul_sparse.md:43
msgid ""
"from examples.gemm_sp.sparse_utils import compress\n"
"A_sparse, E = compress(A)                        # default: int16 metadata "
"for fp16/bf16\n"
"A_sparse, E = compress(A.t().contiguous())       # compress the transposed "
"layout\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deeplearning_operators/matmul_sparse.md:49
msgid ""
"Here, `A_sparse` contains all the non-zero elements of `A`, while `E` stores "
"the corresponding metadata (indexing information) required to reconstruct "
"the original sparse pattern. The metadata uses a natural row-major layout "
"that `T.gemm_sp` consumes directly — no additional layout annotation is "
"needed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deeplearning_operators/matmul_sparse.md:51
msgid "`T.gemm_sp`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deeplearning_operators/matmul_sparse.md:53
msgid ""
"A 2:4 sparse GEMM kernel is similar to its dense counterpart, except that it "
"also requires loading the metadata into shared memory and passing it to `T."
"gemm_sp`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deeplearning_operators/matmul_sparse.md:55
msgid ""
"The default metadata dtype for fp16/bf16 is `int16` with an E-factor of 16 "
"(one `int16` value covers 16 K-elements). For int8/float8 the default is "
"`int32` with E-factor 32."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deeplearning_operators/matmul_sparse.md:57
msgid ""
"import tilelang.language as T\n"
"from examples.gemm_sp.sparse_utils import get_e_factor\n"
"\n"
"def matmul_sp(\n"
"    M, N, K,\n"
"    block_M, block_N, block_K,\n"
"    in_dtype, accum_dtype, e_dtype,\n"
"    num_stages, threads,\n"
"    policy=T.GemmWarpPolicy.Square,\n"
"):\n"
"    e_factor = get_e_factor(in_dtype, e_dtype)\n"
"\n"
"    @T.prim_func\n"
"    def main(\n"
"        A_sparse: T.Tensor((M, K // 2), in_dtype),\n"
"        E: T.Tensor((M, K // e_factor), e_dtype),\n"
"        B: T.Tensor((K, N), in_dtype),\n"
"        C: T.Tensor((M, N), accum_dtype),\n"
"    ):\n"
"        with T.Kernel(T.ceildiv(N, block_N), T.ceildiv(M, block_M), "
"threads=threads) as (bx, by):\n"
"            A_shared = T.alloc_shared((block_M, block_K // 2), in_dtype)\n"
"            B_shared = T.alloc_shared((block_K, block_N), in_dtype)\n"
"            E_shared = T.alloc_shared((block_M, block_K // e_factor), "
"e_dtype)\n"
"            C_local = T.alloc_fragment((block_M, block_N), accum_dtype)\n"
"            C_shared = T.alloc_shared((block_M, block_N), accum_dtype)\n"
"            T.clear(C_local)\n"
"            for k in T.Pipelined(T.ceildiv(K, block_K), "
"num_stages=num_stages):\n"
"                T.copy(A_sparse[by * block_M, k * block_K // 2], A_shared)\n"
"                T.copy(E[by * block_M, k * block_K // e_factor], E_shared)\n"
"                T.copy(B[k * block_K, bx * block_N], B_shared)\n"
"                T.gemm_sp(A_shared, E_shared, B_shared, C_local,\n"
"                          transpose_A=False, transpose_E=False, "
"transpose_B=False,\n"
"                          policy=policy)\n"
"            T.copy(C_local, C_shared)\n"
"            T.copy(C_shared, C[by * block_M, bx * block_N])\n"
"\n"
"    return main\n"
msgstr ""
